## **Client Snapshot**

• Industry, company size, business model
• Brand posture (e.g., disruptor, legacy, value-led)
• 2–4 strategic initiatives or transformation goals
• Named stakeholders & roles (Decision Power: H/M/L)

---

## **Pain Points & Opportunity Areas**

• 3–6 core challenges (include 1–2 verbatim quotes from notes if available)
• Strategic whitespace or unmet needs
• External pressures (market shifts, tech, regulation)

---

## **Our Angle of Attack**

• Lead narrative (e.g., “unlock predictive CX,” “reduce friction at scale”)
• What we are proposing and how it maps to their goals
• Why this is differentiated and timely (capability, timing, proof)

---

## **Known Competitors & Positioning Strategy**

• Who else is likely to pitch and their likely narrative
• Our counters and differentiation (2–4 bullets)

---

## **Strategic Allies & Relationships**

• Past engagements, executive ties, champions
• Third-party partners who can be activated

---

## **Value Proposition for the Client**

• Expected business impact framed in client KPIs
• 2–4 measurable or directional value statements
• Mark as [Assumption] when inferred

---

## **Stakeholder Map (Table)**

